      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "1. Meaning and Importance of DPSP"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "Directive Principles of State Policy (DPSP) provide guidelines for state governance and socio-economic policy.",
        "DPSPs are classified into three major categories: Socialist Principles, Gandhian Principles, and Liberal–Intellectual Principles.",
        "Understanding the key differences between Fundamental Rights and DPSP is crucial for polity preparation."
      ],
